# UI test: a `tool` with no description (SC0190).
#
# `mcp-servers.md` Decision 5 makes this the only construct in Science for
# which documentation is mandatory, and the message has to carry the reason or
# it becomes "document your code" — a style rule a compiler has no business
# enforcing. The reason is narrow: everywhere else a doc comment is read by
# someone who has already decided to call the function, and here it is read by
# the caller *in order to* decide. The second note is the other half: an
# undescribed tool does not error, it is simply never chosen, and no test
# catches that.
#
# The `#` comments above this line are ordinary comments and not `##` runs, so
# they document nothing — which is what makes this file's `tool` undescribed.

tool fit_peaks(run: String, window_lower: F64) -> Int:
    0
